[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5501452101","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123086#issuecomment-5501452101","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123086","id":5501452101,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR-l_RQ","user":{"login":"Alexander-Kashapovich","id":167694496,"node_id":"U_kgDOCf7QoA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167694496?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich","html_url":"https://github.com/Alexander-Kashapovich","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T22:47:22Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T01:03:31Z","body":"<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2b19678a-3ddf-4941-8a87-70197d05d526\" />\n\nReal case: i need to make \"inner hidden room\" in deep of side-view 2D. Nav. Region of this room is definetly fully included in the main region. So i have to find some points where map baking catches this link for every room instance.\n\n_upd: Now i understand that we cant specify the finish's (target) layer mask, so its impossibe in current nav.server. But strange behavior of link, when regions have partial intersections, remains.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5501452101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5529791060","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123086#issuecomment-5529791060","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123086","id":5529791060,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSZnqVA","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T17:48:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T17:51:53Z","body":"A navigation map always merges the entire geometry, including links, no matter what.\nThe layers are for filtering inside queries, not for the map state or how it merges geometry, including links.\n\nYou cant stack and overlap 2d navmeshes inside the same navigation map, it creates invalid geometry.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5529791060/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5532389188","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123086#issuecomment-5532389188","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123086","id":5532389188,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABScGPRA","user":{"login":"Alexander-Kashapovich","id":167694496,"node_id":"U_kgDOCf7QoA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167694496?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich","html_url":"https://github.com/Alexander-Kashapovich","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alexander-Kashapovich/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T21:29:44Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T21:30:33Z","body":"Okay, i reformulate question. Why some positions of link is legal, but another illegal? See pics, i move only start_pos and end_pos of link. If its UB - just say that. Agent who requests query on left sied, target (marker2d) on right side.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/18805902-e886-43fc-809c-4a8f489f85f7\" />\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9f49161c-7b26-4755-a2e5-d891461c8b3e\" />\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c8863911-e0e5-4743-8a05-64811221e35e\" />\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f58abfb8-136c-4cc0-b041-22543eea89bd\" />\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5ec5d4c9-927a-4cc5-a4ad-26edcdc81820\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5532389188/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5594850525","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123086#issuecomment-5594850525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123086","id":5594850525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTXqk3Q","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T02:27:56Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T02:32:48Z","body":"Links search within their connection radius for a valid navmesh polygon. If one is found they connect on the closest edge of that polygon.\n\nFor pathfindng corridor building the search travels from closest edge point to closest edge point so by moving positions around that shifts what gets selected.\n\nConnections are also established in a loop, so not only does the edge distance affect what gets selected but also the internal order of polygons and links affect how things are merged and selected.\n\nBy causing navmesh geometry overlap all bets are off how things end up at the internal because each region by default updates async same as the map, so you can hardly predict any order reliably.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5594850525/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]